rs/g199209/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/g199209/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/g199209/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/g199209/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/g199209/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/g199209","user_view_type":"public"}}],"issue":{"active_lock_reason":null,"assignee":null,"assignees":[],"author_association":"NONE","body":"### Description\n\nI have installed `jax[cuda12]`, but not all hosts have GPU, so I want to use CPU on there machines.\r\n\r\nI tried to use this way first:\r\n\r\n```python\r\ndef jax_force_use_cpu_v1():\r\n    os.environ[\"JAX_PLATFORMS\"] = \"cpu\"\r\n    jax.config.update(\"jax_platform_name\", 'cpu')\r\n\r\njax_force_use_cpu_v1()\r\n```\r\n\r\nBut this hasn't work:\r\n\r\n```\r\nRuntimeError: Unable to initialize backend 'cuda': FAILED_PRECONDITION: No visible GPU devices. (you may need to uninstall the failing plugin package, or set JAX_PLATFORMS=cpu to skip this backend.)\r\n```\r\n\r\nI found another workaround later:\r\n\r\n```python\r\ndef jax_force_use_cpu_v2():\r\n    try:\r\n        jax.lib.xla_bridge.get_backend()\r\n    except RuntimeError:\r\n        pass\r\n\r\njax_force_use_cpu_v2()\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis works but it looks weird. I'm not sure is this the correct way to do it?\n\n### System info (python version, jaxlib version, accelerator, etc.)\n\njax varsion: 0.4.30","closed_at":"2024-08-23T03:44:09Z","closed_by":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/14262417?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yashk2810/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yashk2810/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yashk2810/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yashk2810/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/yashk2810","id":14262417,"login":"yashk28